	(descr "Generic commodity SMD gull-wing DIP-4 phototransistor optocoupler land pattern, used by onsemi FOD817DS (DigiKey Package/Case: '4-SMD, Gull Wing'; Supplier Device Package: '4-SMD'; LCSC/onsemi call the package family 'SMD-4P') and its near-identical commodity siblings (PC817X0NSZ0F, EL817S(TA), LTV-817S, etc. -- these SMD-gull-wing DIP-4 optocouplers share a de-facto standard body/lead form). Placeholder name 'Package_DIP:DIP-4_W7.62mm_SMDGullWing' does not exist in stock KiCad10 (Package_DIP.pretty only has DIP-4_W7.62mm THT and DIP-4_W7.62mm_SMDSocket_SmallPads; a broad case-insensitive search for *gull*/*gullwing* across the ENTIRE stock footprint tree returned zero hits). Dimensions used: body 6.5x4.0mm (commonly cited across FOD817/PC817/EL817 SMD-gull-wing datasheets), 2.54mm (0.1in) pin pitch along each row (pins 1-2 and 4-3), foot-tip-to-foot-tip row span ~9.8mm (typical formed gull-wing span for this commodity 300mil-body package family; onsemi's own FOD817DS numeric land-pattern table could not be retrieved in machine-readable form -- WebFetch of the onsemi/Mouser PDF returned only package-suffix text, not the dimension table). APPROXIMATION FLAGGED: exact body width/pad foot length may vary +/-0.3mm between onsemi's actual FOD817DS drawing and this generic commodity value; verify against onsemi's FOD817 datasheet package outline before fab if tolerance is critical.")
	(tags "FOD817DS optocoupler DIP-4 SMD gull wing SOP-4")
